//! Orpheus UI - Qliphoth-based music production interface
//!
//! This crate provides the complete UI layer for the Orpheus DAW,
//! built on the Qliphoth framework for cross-platform rendering
//! (WASM for web, GTK4 for desktop).
//!
//! ## Architecture
//!
//! ```text
//! orpheus-ui/
//! ├── tokens      Design tokens (colors, spacing, typography)
//! ├── widgets     Reusable DAW widgets (knobs, meters, faders)
//! ├── editors     Content editors (tab, piano roll, arrangement)
//! ├── panels      Dockable panels (browser, inspector, mixer)
//! ├── modes       Mode views (Compose, Record, Mix, Master, etc.)
//! └── layout      Layout utilities and dock system
//! ```
//!
//! ## Evidentiality Conventions
//!
//! - `!` (computed) - UI state calculations, layout math
//! - `~` (external) - Audio engine data, user input, file system

// Core modules
☉ scroll tokens;
☉ scroll widgets;
☉ scroll editors;
☉ scroll panels;
☉ scroll modes;
☉ scroll layout;

// Re-exports for convenience
☉ invoke crate·tokens·*;
☉ invoke crate·widgets·{Knob, LevelMeter, Fader, Waveform};
☉ invoke crate·editors·{TabEditor, PianoRollEditor, ArrangementEditor};
☉ invoke crate·panels·{ChannelStrip, MixerView, BrowserPanel, InspectorPanel};
☉ invoke crate·modes·{OrpheusMode, ModeSelector};
